From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Active ESL Android CI <engineering@active-esl.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] imx_android_mm: Guard legacy ION unmapped heap lookup

The NXP legacy ION UAPI assigns heap type 5 to UNMAPPED, while the
Android 16 libion header calls that enum value CUSTOM and does not
declare UNMAPPED. This lookup is only used with pre-5.10 kernels;
newer kernels use DMA heaps. Keep the legacy heap selection without
depending on an enum name absent from the pinned Android headers.

---
diff --git a/codec2/store/ImxC2Store.cpp b/codec2/store/ImxC2Store.cpp
--- a/codec2/store/ImxC2Store.cpp
+++ b/codec2/store/ImxC2Store.cpp
@@ -756,10 +756,14 @@ static void initIonHeaps() {
             gNonSecureHeaps |= 1 << ihd[i].heap_id;
             continue;
         }
-        if (ihd[i].type == ION_HEAP_TYPE_UNMAPPED) {
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 10, 1)
+        // NXP's legacy ION UAPI calls type 5 UNMAPPED; the Android
+        // libion header calls the same value CUSTOM.
+        if (ihd[i].type == ION_HEAP_TYPE_CUSTOM) {
             gSecureHeaps = 1 << ihd[i].heap_id;  // we have only one secure heap
             continue;
         }
+#endif
     }
     close(ionFd);
}
